MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-04-12T11:52:57Z","updated_at":"2025-04-13T14:25:19Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: Godot v4.4.stable.official [4c311cbee]\n\n### System information\n\nUbuntu Linux 22.04\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen trying to obtain a parent of a directory (e.g. by concatenating a directory with `../`), get_current_dir() returns a relative and not an absolute path, which is in contradiction to the documentation:\n\n> Returns the absolute path to the currently opened directory (e.g. `res://folder` or `C:\\tmp\\folder`).\n\nThis problem does not happen on Windows.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThe following prints `/home/..` instead of `/` on Linux.\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node2D\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tprint(DirAccess.open(\"/home/..\").get_current_dir(false))\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[get-current-dir-repro.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19719421/get-current-dir-repro.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105312/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105312/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}